      68 +session-signed attestation (honored only where the rite sets   
      69 +`allow_waivers = true`).                                       
      70  
      71 +## The session key can live in memory only                     
      72 +                                                               
      73 +By default the session seed is a file (`session.key`, destroyed
         + at shred). A                                                  
      74 +file that outlives a crashed session is a liability: the next s
         +ession's open                                                  
      75 +rite reads as done, and the key could sign as its dead owner — 
         +`status` warns                                                 
      76 +whenever a key is sitting on disk. Set `session_key = "ephemera
         +l"` in                                                         
      77 +`comms.toml` and the seed never touches disk at all: `mint` sho
         +ws it exactly                                                  
      78 +once, later steps read it from `COMMS_SESSION_SEED` in the hold
         +er's                                                           
      79 +environment (it must derive the recorded session id, so a wrong
         + seed cannot                                                   
      80 +quietly sign), and the shred is the holder unsetting and forget
         +ting it — the                                                  
      81 +tool reports the step done only once no environment can produce
         + the seed. A                                                   
      82 +crashed ephemeral session's seed dies with it. The trade: the s
         +eed passes                                                     
      83 +through the holder's memory and environment, so a holder whose 
         +own context is                                                 
      84 +recorded (e.g. an agent transcript) should prefer the file mode
         + and shred at                                                  
      85 +close.                                                         
      86 +                                                               
      87  ## The stance
      88  
      89  Verification here means the math holds, not that trust has been
           decided. The

