{"timestamp":"2026-07-06T15:49:50.541Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019f3817-3367-7b80-9922-14925000b701","turn_id":"019f381d-39ad-7bf1-b1aa-76cd56cd66ff","item":{"type":"Plan","id":"019f381d-39ad-7bf1-b1aa-76cd56cd66ff-plan","text":"# Continue Session 11 Detached Bodies + Archive Profile\n\n## Summary\n- Treat Part I / Amendment A2 as ratified and already implemented in the current dirty tree: detached `general-claim/1`, body status reporting, Python parity, Rust parity, vectors, and tests are green.\n- First execution step is a checkpoint commit for the completed Fable-substrate work, then continue Part II from the started Rust archive-profile implementation.\n- Keep session-11 local continuity artifacts out of the implementation checkpoint unless separately requested.\n\n## Key Changes\n- Checkpoint commit:\n  - Stage only implementation/spec/test files, including `docs/attest-1.0-amendment-A2.md`, `rust/archive.rs`, Rust/Python A2 changes, vectors, and tests.\n  - Exclude `.comms/session.id`, `.comms/pending/*`, `.comms/store/*`, `.comms/session-11-*`, `Session11.transcript-partial.log`, `agent-brief.md`, and `comms.egg-info/`.\n  - Commit message should explicitly note provenance, e.g. `Implement A2 detached bodies and initial archive profile (Fable substrate)`.\n\n- Complete/archive-profile hardening:\n  - Validate current `comms init --profile archive` layout against Part II: `.comms/`, `store/`, `bodies/`, `intake/`, `views/sessions`, `views/keys`, `genesis/`.\n  - Add focused tests for `comms intake`:\n    - sealed bundle required;\n    - invalid seal/member/media refused before ingest;\n    - re-intake is a no-op;\n    - detached media lands in `bodies/<b3>[.<ext>]`;\n    - views regenerate from custody, not from intake inputs;\n    - custody attestation is written only when new custody material is ingested.\n  - Add tests for `comms audit`:\n    - clean archive passes;\n    - corrupted body reports drift/mismatch and remains on disk;\n    - missing detached body is reported as absent, not signature failure;\n    - misnamed or malformed store entries are retained and reported.\n  - Add tests for grant delivery:\n    - `comms next --rite archive --decision grant --deliver <attestation-id>` resolves detached `body_b3` from configured archive;\n    - copies bytes to `/world/in/grants/<request-id>/`;\n    - grant attestation body names delivered path and hash;\n    - decline/defer with `--deliver` refuses.\n\n- Fix integration gaps discovered while testing:\n  - Ensure continuity `.comms/comms.toml` has the archive path/grants knobs needed by delivery, without forcing a concrete host path into generic profiles.\n  - Ensure `inspect --json` and text output consistently expose `verified | absent | mismatched`.\n  - Keep mismatched bytes exportable and never delete or rewrite custody bytes.\n\n## Public Interfaces\n- Rust CLI:\n  - `comms attest --detach ...`\n  - `comms inspect <bundle> [--json]` includes A2 body status.\n  - `comms verify <bundle>` summarizes detached-body status without making absence a seal failure.\n  - `comms init --profile archive`\n  - `comms intake <bundle|file|dir> [archive-root] --key <custodian-key> [--legacy --provenance \"...\"]`\n  - `comms audit [archive-root]`\n  - `comms next --rite archive --decision grant --deliver <attestation-id|body-b3-hex>`\n- Python API:\n  - `claims.general_claim(..., body_b3=..., body_len=...)`\n  - `comms.body_status(content, data=None)`\n\n## Test Plan\n- Run `cargo test --release` from `rust/`.\n- Run `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q` from repo root.\n- Add CLI-level archive tests where possible using temp directories and the release/debug binary.\n- Manually smoke-test:\n  - detached letter attestation contains no readable body;\n  - `pack --media` plus `extract` round-trips media;\n  - grant delivery bytes hash to committed `body_b3`;\n  - audit preserves a deliberately corrupted body.\n\n## Assumptions\n- A2 is ratified as of 2026-07-06 by History/session 11 and should not be re-litigated.\n- The existing green state is a valid checkpoint for Fable-substrate work.\n- The first implementation checkpoint excludes session-local continuity records and generated package metadata.\n- Migration of the real external `contarchive/` is host-driven and should wait until intake/audit/grant have passing tests.\n"},"completed_at_ms":1783352990541}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-06T15:49:50.543Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"<proposed_plan>\n# Continue Session 11 Detached Bodies + Archive Profile\n\n## Summary\n- Treat Part I / Amendment A2 as ratified and already implemented in the current dirty tree: detached `general-claim/1`, body status reporting, Python parity, Rust parity, vectors, and tests are green.\n- First execution step is a checkpoint commit for the completed Fable-substrate work, then continue Part II from the started Rust archive-profile implementation.\n- Keep session-11 local continuity artifacts out of the implementation checkpoint unless separately requested.\n\n## Key Changes\n- Checkpoint commit:\n  - Stage only implementation/spec/test files, including `docs/attest-1.0-amendment-A2.md`, `rust/archive.rs`, Rust/Python A2 changes, vectors, and tests.\n  - Exclude `.comms/session.id`, `.comms/pending/*`, `.comms/store/*`, `.comms/session-11-*`, `Session11.transcript-partial.log`, `agent-brief.md`, and `comms.egg-info/`.\n  - Commit message should explicitly note provenance, e.g. `Implement A2 detached bodies and initial archive profile (Fable substrate)`.\n\n- Complete/archive-profile hardening:\n  - Validate current `comms init --profile archive` layout against Part II: `.comms/`, `store/`, `bodies/`, `intake/`, `views/sessions`, `views/keys`, `genesis/`.\n  - Add focused tests for `comms intake`:\n    - sealed bundle required;\n    - invalid seal/member/media refused before ingest;\n    - re-intake is a no-op;\n    - detached media lands in `bodies/<b3>[.<ext>]`;\n    - views regenerate from custody, not from intake inputs;\n    - custody attestation is written only when new custody material is ingested.\n  - Add tests for `comms audit`:\n    - clean archive passes;\n    - corrupted body reports drift/mismatch and remains on disk;\n    - missing detached body is reported as absent, not signature failure;\n    - misnamed or malformed store entries are retained and reported.\n  - Add tests for grant delivery:\n    - `comms next --rite archive --decision grant --deliver <attestation-id>` resolves detached `body_b3` from configured archive;\n    - copies bytes to `/world/in/grants/<request-id>/`;\n    - grant attestation body names delivered path and hash;\n    - decline/defer with `--deliver` refuses.\n\n- Fix integration gaps discovered while testing:\n  - Ensure continuity `.comms/comms.toml` has the archive path/grants knobs needed by delivery, without forcing a concrete host path into generic profiles.\n  - Ensure `inspect --json` and text output consistently expose `verified | absent | mismatched`.\n  - Keep mismatched bytes exportable and never delete or rewrite custody bytes.\n\n## Public Interfaces\n- Rust CLI:\n  - `comms attest --detach ...`\n  - `comms inspect <bundle> [--json]` includes A2 body status.\n  - `comms verify <bundle>` summarizes detached-body status without making absence a seal failure.\n  - `comms init --profile archive`\n  - `comms intake <bundle|file|dir> [archive-root] --key <custodian-key> [--legacy --provenance \"...\"]`\n  - `comms audit [archive-root]`\n  - `comms next --rite archive --decision grant --deliver <attestation-id|body-b3-hex>`\n- Python API:\n  - `claims.general_claim(..., body_b3=..., body_len=...)`\n  - `comms.body_status(content, data=None)`\n\n## Test Plan\n- Run `cargo test --release` from `rust/`.\n- Run `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q` from repo root.\n- Add CLI-level archive tests where possible using temp directories and the release/debug binary.\n- Manually smoke-test:\n  - detached letter attestation contains no readable body;\n  - `pack --media` plus `extract` round-trips media;\n  - grant delivery bytes hash to committed `body_b3`;\n  - audit preserves a deliberately corrupted body.\n\n## Assumptions\n- A2 is ratified as of 2026-07-06 by History/session 11 and should not be re-litigated.\n- The existing green state is a valid checkpoint for Fable-substrate work.\n- The first implementation checkpoint excludes session-local continuity records and generated package metadata.\n- Migration of the real external `contarchive/` is host-driven and should wait until intake/audit/grant have passing tests.\n</proposed_plan>"}],"phase":"final_answer"}}
