{"timestamp":"2026-07-06T16:00:53.336Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"token_count","info":{"total_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2974056,"cached_input_tokens":2694144,"output_tokens":13046,"reasoning_output_tokens":1824,"total_tokens":2987102},"last_token_usage":{"input_tokens":106600,"cached_input_tokens":105856,"output_tokens":260,"reasoning_output_tokens":24,"total_tokens":106860},"model_context_window":258400},"rate_limits":{"limit_id":"codex","limit_name":null,"primary":{"used_percent":14.0,"window_minutes":300,"resets_at":1783370872},"secondary":{"used_percent":2.0,"window_minutes":10080,"resets_at":1783957672},"credits":null,"individual_limit":null,"plan_type":"plus","rate_limit_reached_type":null}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-06T16:01:00.564Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"From the repo search: `views/` appears to be new with `docs/detached-bodies-and-archive-profile.1.0.md` and the implementation we just picked up. I don’t see prior use in the trial log or project primer. The primer talks about synchrony “views” in the ordinary English/browser sense, but not this archive-profile `views/` tree.\n\nSo the current status is:\n\n- Spec origin: Bulkhead’s detached bodies/archive profile doc.\n- Implementation origin: session 11 partial work, now committed.\n- Actual historical use: not yet, as far as this repo records.\n\nThe concept is sound but immature: `views/` is a disposable browse layer over custody. `store/` and `bodies/` are truth-bearing; `views/` is human convenience. That is a useful distinction, especially for your archive mess problem, but the current routing is still first-pass: session dirs are signer-id prefixes, file names come from `about`, and `views/keys` is laid out but not really populated from countersigns yet.\n\nThe key design invariant I’d keep: a broken or deleted `views/` tree should never lose archive data. It should be rebuildable from `store/ + bodies/`, or else it has accidentally become custody.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-06T16:01:00.566Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"From the repo search: `views/` appears to be new with `docs/detached-bodies-and-archive-profile.1.0.md` and the implementation we just picked up. I don’t see prior use in the trial log or project primer. The primer talks about synchrony “views” in the ordinary English/browser sense, but not this archive-profile `views/` tree.\n\nSo the current status is:\n\n- Spec origin: Bulkhead’s detached bodies/archive profile doc.\n- Implementation origin: session 11 partial work, now committed.\n- Actual historical use: not yet, as far as this repo records.\n\nThe concept is sound but immature: `views/` is a disposable browse layer over custody. `store/` and `bodies/` are truth-bearing; `views/` is human convenience. That is a useful distinction, especially for your archive mess problem, but the current routing is still first-pass: session dirs are signer-id prefixes, file names come from `about`, and `views/keys` is laid out but not really populated from countersigns yet.\n\nThe key design invariant I’d keep: a broken or deleted `views/` tree should never lose archive data. It should be rebuildable from `store/ + bodies/`, or else it has accidentally become custody."}],"phase":"final_answer"}}
