{"timestamp":"2026-07-06T16:01:00.607Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"task_complete","turn_id":"019f3829-18c8-77f0-ad38-b24fdbeb9a8d","last_agent_message":"From the repo search: `views/` appears to be new with `docs/detached-bodies-and-archive-profile.1.0.md` and the implementation we just picked up. I don’t see prior use in the trial log or project primer. The primer talks about synchrony “views” in the ordinary English/browser sense, but not this archive-profile `views/` tree.\n\nSo the current status is:\n\n- Spec origin: Bulkhead’s detached bodies/archive profile doc.\n- Implementation origin: session 11 partial work, now committed.\n- Actual historical use: not yet, as far as this repo records.\n\nThe concept is sound but immature: `views/` is a disposable browse layer over custody. `store/` and `bodies/` are truth-bearing; `views/` is human convenience. That is a useful distinction, especially for your archive mess problem, but the current routing is still first-pass: session dirs are signer-id prefixes, file names come from `about`, and `views/keys` is laid out but not really populated from countersigns yet.\n\nThe key design invariant I’d keep: a broken or deleted `views/` tree should never lose archive data. It should be rebuildable from `store/ + bodies/`, or else it has accidentally become custody.","completed_at":1783353660,"duration_ms":15350,"time_to_first_token_ms":3550}}
