{"timestamp":"2026-07-06T16:12:41.902Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"task_complete","turn_id":"019f3833-a7c4-7412-8c59-657eb1e38980","last_agent_message":"Added the README note:\n\n```text\nIf Comms or the Continuity Trial influenced your system, we would appreciate a note or link, but it is not required.\nMessage us if you need anything.\n```\n\nFor drift custody attestations, I’d make `audit` produce a **suggested next command** whenever it finds drift, not automatically sign anything by default.\n\nThe logic:\n\n1. `comms audit` walks `store/` and `bodies/`.\n2. It classifies findings:\n   - `store-drift`: unparseable, misnamed, bad id, bad signature.\n   - `body-mismatched`: body filename claims hash X, bytes now hash Y.\n   - `body-absent`: detached attestation commits to X, but no body in custody.\n   - `unreferenced-body`: body exists but no current store attestation commits to it.\n3. It writes a machine-readable draft report, maybe:\n   - `audit/YYYYMMDDTHHMMSSZ.drift.json`\n   - plus `audit/YYYYMMDDTHHMMSSZ.drift.md`\n4. If there are drift findings, stdout ends with exact commands:\n\n```sh\ncomms audit-attest audit/20260706T193012Z.drift.json --key <custodian-key>\n```\n\nor, if folded into `audit`:\n\n```sh\ncomms audit --attest audit/20260706T193012Z.drift.json --key <custodian-key>\n```\n\nThe attestation should be a `general-claim/1` with kind like `archive-drift-custody`, about `archive`, and body containing the audit report. It should **not** claim repair. It says: “At this time, custody contained these mismatches/absences; mismatched bytes were retained.”\n\nI’d make the suggestion deterministic and conservative: same archive state produces same draft report except timestamp. The signed body should include paths, expected hash, actual hash/len where readable, relevant attestation ids, and explicit preservation language.\n\nBest CLI feel:\n\n```text\ndrift found. nothing was deleted or repaired.\n\nnext:\n  review audit/20260706T193012Z.drift.md\n  comms audit-attest audit/20260706T193012Z.drift.json --key <custodian-key>\n```\n\nThat preserves the nice rite pattern: the tool does not decide the custodian’s testimony, but it makes the honest next act obvious.","completed_at":1783354361,"duration_ms":24678,"time_to_first_token_ms":3275}}
