{"timestamp":"2026-07-06T16:31:47.766Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"sound logic. what would be the draft report structure? (ie fields captured)  is the json for machines and the .md for human readers? the classifications seem comprehensive and the naming style is lucid. stdout with exact commands just like in other comms rite sequences. CLI feel's good. You are right about the archive role boundary being awkward, if not confused. CLI feel should be different when i'm doing archive work on the host versus when the vm based entity staging things for the archive is working. Let's improve how the door traverses the wall from both sides."}]}}
