{"timestamp":"2026-07-06T16:34:00.804Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"Implemented and committed as `50402b8 Clarify archive wall crossing roles`.\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- README now has the soft acknowledgement request plus: “Message us if you need anything.”\n- `docs/detached-bodies-and-archive-profile.1.0.md` now defines:\n  - **Two doors, one wall**\n  - repo/session side: author, request, stage, seal, export\n  - host/archive side: verify, ingest, audit, attest custody, deliver\n  - `views/` as **undurable projections**\n  - audit drift draft reports: JSON for machines, Markdown for human review\n- Generated `.comms` door/config text now distinguishes:\n  - repo-side archive client config\n  - archive-side custody root config\n- CLI help for `intake`/`audit` now uses host/archive-side language and says audit should propose custody testimony on drift.\n\nThe draft report structure I encoded has `schema`, `archive_root`, `audited_at`, tool/version, summary counts, and `findings[]` with classes:\n\n- `body-mismatched`\n- `body-absent`\n- `store-drift`\n- `unreferenced-body`\n\nEach finding carries the relevant path, expected/actual hashes and lengths when available, referencing attestation ids when known, and `disposition` like `retained` or `absent`.\n\nVerification passed before commit:\n\n- `cargo test --release`\n- `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q`\n\nRemaining dirty state is still only the session-local `.comms` artifacts, transcript/brief, and `comms.egg-info`, as intended.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-06T16:34:00.806Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Implemented and committed as `50402b8 Clarify archive wall crossing roles`.\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- README now has the soft acknowledgement request plus: “Message us if you need anything.”\n- `docs/detached-bodies-and-archive-profile.1.0.md` now defines:\n  - **Two doors, one wall**\n  - repo/session side: author, request, stage, seal, export\n  - host/archive side: verify, ingest, audit, attest custody, deliver\n  - `views/` as **undurable projections**\n  - audit drift draft reports: JSON for machines, Markdown for human review\n- Generated `.comms` door/config text now distinguishes:\n  - repo-side archive client config\n  - archive-side custody root config\n- CLI help for `intake`/`audit` now uses host/archive-side language and says audit should propose custody testimony on drift.\n\nThe draft report structure I encoded has `schema`, `archive_root`, `audited_at`, tool/version, summary counts, and `findings[]` with classes:\n\n- `body-mismatched`\n- `body-absent`\n- `store-drift`\n- `unreferenced-body`\n\nEach finding carries the relevant path, expected/actual hashes and lengths when available, referencing attestation ids when known, and `disposition` like `retained` or `absent`.\n\nVerification passed before commit:\n\n- `cargo test --release`\n- `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q`\n\nRemaining dirty state is still only the session-local `.comms` artifacts, transcript/brief, and `comms.egg-info`, as intended."}],"phase":"final_answer"}}
