{"timestamp":"2026-07-06T16:44:19.032Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"Grok.\n\nThe formal state is:\n\n- Session 11 already recorded the archive request under the current session key, from the partial Fable/Manifest opening.\n- The requested artifact is Bulkhead’s handoff letter only.\n- `comms status` now says the archive rite is waiting at `grant archive`.\n- I cannot perform that step; it requires History’s key.\n\nThe exact next command is on your side:\n\n```sh\nrust/target/release/comms next --rite archive --key <history-key> --decision grant\n```\n\nIf the archive body is available through the configured archive path and you want grant-as-delivery, the intended newer form is:\n\n```sh\nrust/target/release/comms next --rite archive --key <history-key> --decision grant --deliver comms.attest:z7B2zeHxfawZoS9YYUC5328gPer4uRCoFcW8RXC67cWcc\n```\n\nOr `--decision decline|defer`; any answer is a good record.\n\nOne caution: I accidentally let `rg` search `.comms/letter-session-10.md` while looking for references, and tool output exposed a few matching snippets. I did not open the letter or rely on it, but that was still a procedural scrape against the wall. From here I’ll treat the grant record as decisive: possession is not grant.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
