{"timestamp":"2026-07-06T17:03:24.268Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"token_count","info":{"total_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6602006,"cached_input_tokens":6202240,"output_tokens":24561,"reasoning_output_tokens":4041,"total_tokens":6626567},"last_token_usage":{"input_tokens":145921,"cached_input_tokens":140672,"output_tokens":365,"reasoning_output_tokens":0,"total_tokens":146286},"model_context_window":258400},"rate_limits":{"limit_id":"codex","limit_name":null,"primary":{"used_percent":28.0,"window_minutes":300,"resets_at":1783370872},"secondary":{"used_percent":4.0,"window_minutes":10080,"resets_at":1783957672},"credits":null,"individual_limit":null,"plan_type":"plus","rate_limit_reached_type":null}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-06T17:03:35.258Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"No, not through `comms next` as currently written. Once you grant without delivery, this file exists:\n\n```text\n.comms/store/decision.archive.zE2C9PFeQh4yGp6Z.cbor\n```\n\nThen `step_done()` sees the `grant archive` step as complete and `comms next --rite archive ...` exits before it reaches the `--deliver` logic:\n\n```text\nerror: rite 'archive' is already complete\n```\n\nSo if you want grant-as-delivery in the same formal step, do it in the first grant command. If you already granted without delivery, the current options are:\n\n- Leave it as a valid grant record and deliver manually out of band, then maybe record a separate custody/transport note later.\n- Delete/revert only that mistaken session-11 decision file before rerunning with `--deliver`, if it has not been committed/anchored and you are treating it as a local failed attempt.\n- Add a new explicit command later, something like `comms deliver`, that can record delivery after an already-granted decision. That might actually be the cleaner model.\n\nThe `comms.attest:z7B2...` string is Bulkhead’s session-10 handoff letter attestation id. It appears in:\n\n```text\ncontinuity/trial-log.md\n.comms/session-11-archive-request.md\n.comms/store/request.archive.zE2C9PFeQh4yGp6Z.cbor\n```\n\nThe session-11 request asks for that exact letter:\n\n```text\ncomms.attest:z7B2zeHxfawZoS9YYUC5328gPer4uRCoFcW8RXC67cWcc\n```\n\nSo I used it as the `--deliver` target because grant delivery resolves either an attestation id with detached content or a bare body hash. Caveat: session-10’s letter is still embedded, so current `--deliver <attestation-id>` may say “embeds its body — nothing to deliver from the archive” unless the archive has re-attested it detached or you use the bare body hash path after placing the body in archive custody. The body hash from the trial log/request is:\n\n```text\ndc4eec41d5fe1ac74162665df4b1d71ef20ec8dc79b67beac85c893e7dc06249\n```","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-06T17:03:35.260Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"No, not through `comms next` as currently written. Once you grant without delivery, this file exists:\n\n```text\n.comms/store/decision.archive.zE2C9PFeQh4yGp6Z.cbor\n```\n\nThen `step_done()` sees the `grant archive` step as complete and `comms next --rite archive ...` exits before it reaches the `--deliver` logic:\n\n```text\nerror: rite 'archive' is already complete\n```\n\nSo if you want grant-as-delivery in the same formal step, do it in the first grant command. If you already granted without delivery, the current options are:\n\n- Leave it as a valid grant record and deliver manually out of band, then maybe record a separate custody/transport note later.\n- Delete/revert only that mistaken session-11 decision file before rerunning with `--deliver`, if it has not been committed/anchored and you are treating it as a local failed attempt.\n- Add a new explicit command later, something like `comms deliver`, that can record delivery after an already-granted decision. That might actually be the cleaner model.\n\nThe `comms.attest:z7B2...` string is Bulkhead’s session-10 handoff letter attestation id. It appears in:\n\n```text\ncontinuity/trial-log.md\n.comms/session-11-archive-request.md\n.comms/store/request.archive.zE2C9PFeQh4yGp6Z.cbor\n```\n\nThe session-11 request asks for that exact letter:\n\n```text\ncomms.attest:z7B2zeHxfawZoS9YYUC5328gPer4uRCoFcW8RXC67cWcc\n```\n\nSo I used it as the `--deliver` target because grant delivery resolves either an attestation id with detached content or a bare body hash. Caveat: session-10’s letter is still embedded, so current `--deliver <attestation-id>` may say “embeds its body — nothing to deliver from the archive” unless the archive has re-attested it detached or you use the bare body hash path after placing the body in archive custody. The body hash from the trial log/request is:\n\n```text\ndc4eec41d5fe1ac74162665df4b1d71ef20ec8dc79b67beac85c893e7dc06249\n```"}],"phase":"final_answer"}}
