{"timestamp":"2026-07-06T17:14:11.132Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"That error is good: `comms deliver` is finding the request and archive config, but the body file is not yet in the archive’s `bodies/`.\n\nFor this transitional embedded-letter case, put the letter body into the archive body store under its hash:\n\n```sh\nmkdir -p ../project.comms-archive/bodies\ncp .comms/letter-session-10.md \\\n  ../project.comms-archive/bodies/dc4eec41d5fe1ac74162665df4b1d71ef20ec8dc79b67beac85c893e7dc06249.md\n```\n\nVerify the hash before retrying:\n\n```sh\nb3sum ../project.comms-archive/bodies/dc4eec41d5fe1ac74162665df4b1d71ef20ec8dc79b67beac85c893e7dc06249.md\n```\n\nIt should print:\n\n```text\ndc4eec41d5fe1ac74162665df4b1d71ef20ec8dc79b67beac85c893e7dc06249\n```\n\nThen rerun:\n\n```sh\ncomms deliver dc4eec41d5fe1ac74162665df4b1d71ef20ec8dc79b67beac85c893e7dc06249\n```\n\nWhy this manual copy is needed: session 10’s letter predates detached-body archive intake. The body exists in the repo as `.comms/letter-session-10.md`, but not yet as archive custody under `../project.comms-archive/bodies/<hash>.md`. New detached letters should arrive there via `comms intake`; this one is a bridge case.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
